-- V21 (PLANNED, NOT YET APPLIED — rename .deferred to .sql when ready)
--
-- Unify `reviews` + `series_reviews` into a single polymorphic table,
-- mirroring the pattern already used by `review_replies` + `review_likes`.
--
-- Strategy (blue/green, no downtime):
--   1. Create `reviews_v2(target_type, target_id, ...)` next to existing
--      reviews and series_reviews. Same uniqueness + check rules.
--   2. Backfill from both source tables. The `id` of each row is rewritten
--      so reviews_v2.id space is fresh (BIGSERIAL). Keep a mapping table
--      `_reviews_v2_mapping(legacy_kind, legacy_id, new_id)` so the
--      reviewsocial.target_id polymorphic FKs (in review_likes,
--      review_replies, notifications) can be retargeted atomically.
--   3. Application toggle: read from reviews_v2 first, fall back to legacy.
--   4. Once verified, retarget reviewsocial pointers using the mapping
--      table, drop old `reviews` and `series_reviews`, drop mapping.
--   5. Rename `reviews_v2` → `reviews`.
--
-- DO NOT enable this migration without:
--   * a snapshot/backup of `reviews` and `series_reviews`,
--   * a feature flag in the service layer to route reads,
--   * regression tests covering ReviewSocialEnrichmentService,
--     NotificationListener, ReplyService.
--
-- File suffix `.sql.deferred` keeps Flyway from picking it up. Rename to
-- `V21__reviews_polymorphic.sql` once the application code is ready.
